  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Determine the slope and $y$-intercept of the line $y=4x-3.$\n\nThe slope of the line is\n{{field-1}}\n and the $y$-intercept is\n{{field-2}}.",
  "worked_solution": "The equation is in slope-intercept form $y=mx+b,$ where $m$ is the slope and $b$ is the $y$-intercept.\n\nFor the equation $y=4x-3,$ we see that the slope is $m=4$ and the $y$-intercept is $b=-3.$",
